            "q": "What Regional Value Content is required for printed circuit assemblies under USMCA?",
            "a": "Under USMCA Chapter 4 (covering HTS Chapters 84, 85, and 90), electronic sub-assemblies and printed circuit assemblies (PCBAs) generally qualify for duty-free entry if they satisfy either a 60% Regional Value Content threshold using the Transaction Value method, or a 50% RVC threshold using the Net Cost method. Alternatively, products can qualify through specific Tariff Shift rules (such as a change in heading or subheading from non-originating components), provided all originating criteria are meticulously documented."
